<title>HUNGARY: Primagaz reports lower op profit for Q1.</title>
<headline>Primagaz reports lower op profit for Q1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three month period ending March 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					 1997		 1996</p>
<p>    Operating profit		550	 vs     622</p>
<p>    Income before taxation	481	 vs     535</p>
<p>    Net income			394	 vs     392</p>
<p>    Sales			   5,525	 vs   4,688</p>
<p>    Cost of sales		 3,341	 vs   2,815</p>
<p>    Gross margin		  2,184	 vs   1,873</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures	472	 vs     428</p>
<p>    Depreciation		    181	 vs     121</p>
<p>    Other expenses		  981	 vs     702</p>
<p>    Interest income		  27	 vs	32</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 95	 vs     132</p>
<p>    Other financial income	  1 loss  vs	13 profit</p>
<p>    Corporate income tax	   87	 vs     143</p>
<p>NOTE - Primagaz Hungaria Rt is a distributor of liquefied petroleum gas (LPG). The figures were calculated in accordance with International Accounting Standards. The 1997 figures are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
